 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, draw a minimum spanning tree for the given graph, and calculate its weight.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/d486df173439fc1e.png\" alt=\"Four graphs. Graph A has four vertices: a, b, c, and d. The edges are labeled as follows: a b, 3; b d, 3; d c, 1; c a, 2; a d, 1; b c, 2. Graph B has five vertices: e, f, g, h, and i. The edges are labeled as follows: e f, 2-thirds; f g, 5-twelfths; g h, 1-twelfth; h i, 3-fourths; i e, 1-fourth; e h, 1-half; eg, 1-sixth; f i, -third; f h, 5-sixths; g i, 1. Graph C has five vertices: i, j, k, m, and n. The curved edges are labeled as follows: km, 20; m n, 30; n j, 40; j i, 50; i k, 10. The straight edges are labeled as follows: k j, 90; k n, 60; m i, 100; m j, 70; n i, 80. Graph d has four vertices; o, p, q, and r. The edges are labeled as follows: o p, 1.7; p q, 4.3; q r, 3.5; r o, 2.9 p r, 3.; o p, 1.2.\">\n",
